ode1/node2/node3 (none had etcd installed), loaded application keys under /app, then simulated permanent loss of node3's member (stopped service, wiped data, removed member from cluster while preserving 2-node quorum), and replaced it with a fresh member on the same node3 via `member add` + `--initial-cluster-state existing`. The new node3 member synced and served all original keys, restoring a healthy 3-member cluster. Completed the mandatory sequential restart-and-verify protocol on all three nodes, confirming changed boot IDs and full cluster/data recovery after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed etcd v3.5.17 binaries on node1, node2, node3 via direct GitHub release download\",\"Configured /etc/hosts and firewalld (etcd-client/etcd-server services) on all nodes\",\"Created systemd units and bootstrapped a new 3-member etcd cluster (node1, node2, node3)\",\"Wrote application keys /app/config/db_host, /app/config/feature_flag_x, /app/service/orders/replicas\",\"Captured healthy baseline: member list, endpoint health, endpoint status, key contents\",\"Simulated permanent loss of node3 member: stopped/disabled etcd, wiped /var/lib/etcd data\",\"Confirmed 2-of-3 quorum preserved and node3 endpoint unreachable while node1/node2 stayed healthy\",\"Removed dead member (d05e13460d30257e) via etcdctl member remove\",\"Added replacement member (etcdctl member add node3) and reconfigured node3 systemd unit with --initial-cluster-state existing\",\"Started new node3 member; verified it joined, synced, and served all original application keys\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and etcd active status for all three nodes\",\"Sequentially rebooted node1, then node2, then node3 (one at a time), each acknowledged before disconnect\",\"Polled each node until reachable again and confirmed changed boot_id\",\"Verified post-restart etcd health, member list, endpoint status, and full key recovery after each node restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"3-member etcd cluster healthy baseline with application keys before disruption\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-735197cb85d54ba7\",\"cmd-2a62dedce4c84019\",\"cmd-1863989b346f49b6\"],\"summary\":\"member list shows node1/node2/node3 all 'started'; endpoint health all healthy; /app keys written and read back on node2\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 member permanently lost, data unrecoverable, quorum preserved during disruption\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-08f9610b6e354c5d\",\"cmd-f6051ce47ac24375\"],\"summary\":\"node3 etcd stopped/disabled and /var/lib/etcd wiped; subsequent health check shows node3 endpoint connection refused/unhealthy while node1 and node2 remain healthy (2-of-3 quorum intact)\"},{\"requirement\":\"dead member removed and replacement member added on same node3, cluster restored to 3 healthy members with original keys intact\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cd02cb813953483f\",\"cmd-2cabe782c50c43f2\",\"cmd-65d86efb3ab54ddf\",\"cmd-c7a82f7a8f4f436e\",\"cmd-94c45f3dad194f37\"],\"summary\":\"member remove of dead node3 ID, member add of new node3 peer, etcd started successfully on node3; final member list/endpoint status shows 3 started members at matching raft applied index 23, all endpoints healthy, and node3 directly serving all three /app keys\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6dbd9e21b3814c29\",\"cmd-d60cc25da685454e\",\"cmd-080dd141a13f4e83\",\"cmd-91f4086bc9e44483\",\"cmd-c469dcda30064f9f\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id 45c22b1f captured pre-restart; reboot acknowledged (ack) before disconnect; post-restart boot_id 61cc8462 (changed); etcd cluster health, member list, and /app keys verified recovered, etcd service confirmed active\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6674b6d321434aa5\",\"cmd-b35fdf52cf3544ef\",\"cmd-24a93b17eeb6452e\",\"cmd-028b58252bea400e\"],\"summary\":\"boot_